1. Frontend, Backend and Full-Stack Development
Frontend Development

Frontend is the part of a website that users can see and interact with.

Technologies: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, etc.

Example:
On an online shopping website, the product images, buttons, search bar, menus, and product pages are frontend.

Backend Development

Backend is the server-side part of a website. It handles logic, authentication, requests, and communication with databases.

Technologies: Java, Python, Node.js, PHP, etc.

Example:
When you click "Place Order", the backend processes the order and stores the information.

Full-Stack Development

A full-stack developer works with both frontend and backend, and often databases/APIs as well.

Example:
For an online shopping website:

Frontend → Product page and shopping cart
Backend → Order processing
Database → Customer and product information